# test_adt_multi_entry_union_declaration — multi-entry union ADT declaration.
# [type [let a] Ok: [value: a] Error: [msg: String]] declares a union with two constructors.
# Both Ok and Error are injected as runtime bindings with their constructor types.
# Calling Ok with value: Int and Error with msg: String both succeed cleanly.
[
  Result: [type [let a] Ok: [value: a] Error: [msg: String]]
  ok-val:  [Result.Ok value: 42]
  err-val: [Result.Error msg: "failed"]
]
=== out
Dict({"Result": Dict({"Ok": Function(value), "Error": Function(msg)}), "ok-val": Variant(Result.Ok, Dict({"value": Int(42)})), "err-val": Variant(Result.Error, Dict({"msg": String("failed")}))})
